---
components: ["DeltaIndicator"]
description: Delta indicator shows a signed change, such as period-over-period growth, with an arrow, a sign, and a color that each convey the direction.
---

<script>
  import { DataTable, Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { DeltaIndicator } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";
</script>

`DeltaIndicator` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead.

## Basic

Set `value` to the change. Positive values point up and read as good. Negative values point down and read as bad.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={128} />
  <DeltaIndicator value={-64} />
  <DeltaIndicator value={0} />
</Stack>

## Direction

### Lower is better

Set `positive` to `"down"` for metrics where a decrease is the good outcome, such as churn, latency, or error rate. Only the color flips. The arrow always follows the sign.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={-320} positive="down" label="p95 latency (ms)" />
  <DeltaIndicator value={45} positive="down" label="p95 latency (ms)" />
</Stack>

### Neutral threshold

Set `threshold` to treat small changes as no change. An absolute change at or below the threshold renders neutral.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.004} format="percent" threshold={0.005} />
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.04} format="percent" threshold={0.005} />
</Stack>

### Missing value

A missing or non-finite `value` renders a dash.

<DeltaIndicator value={undefined} />

## Formatting

### Percent

Set `format` to `"percent"` to treat `value` as a ratio. `0.123` reads as `+12.3%`.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.123} format="percent" />
  <DeltaIndicator value={-0.041} format="percent" />
</Stack>

### Fraction digits

Set `fractionDigits` to control precision.

<DeltaIndicator value={0.12345} format="percent" fractionDigits={2} />

### Full numbers

Large numbers use compact notation by default. Set `compact` to `false` to write them in full.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={12840} />
  <DeltaIndicator value={12840} compact={false} />
</Stack>

### Number format options

Pass [Intl.NumberFormat options](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/NumberFormat/NumberFormat#options) to `format` for currencies and units.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={1250} format={{ style: "currency", currency: "USD" }} />
  <DeltaIndicator value={-3.5} format={{ style: "unit", unit: "second" }} positive="down" />
</Stack>

### Custom function

Pass a function to `format` for full control. A plus sign is still added to positive values.

<DeltaIndicator value={3} format={(value) => `${value} seats`} />

### Locale

Set `locale` to format for a specific locale.

<DeltaIndicator value={0.1234} format="percent" fractionDigits={2} locale="de-DE" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to match the surrounding text.

<Stack gap={3}>
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.123} format="percent" size="sm" label="Small" />
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.123} format="percent" label="Medium (default)" />
  <DeltaIndicator value={0.123} format="percent" size="lg" label="Large" />
</Stack>

## With label

Set `label` to add trailing context.

<DeltaIndicator value={0.082} format="percent" label="vs last week" />

## Without icon

Set `hideIcon` to drop the arrow. The sign stays, so the direction never rests on color alone.

<DeltaIndicator value={-0.041} format="percent" hideIcon />

## In a data table

Numbers use tabular figures, so deltas line up in a column.

<DataTable
  size="short"
  headers={[
    { key: "name", value: "Service" },
    { key: "requests", value: "Requests" },
    { key: "change", value: "Change" },
  ]}
  rows={[
    { id: "a", name: "api", requests: "1.2M", change: 0.124 },
    { id: "b", name: "checkout", requests: "340K", change: -0.031 },
    { id: "c", name: "search", requests: "2.8M", change: 0.002 },
  ]}
>
  <svelte:fragment slot="cell" let:cell>
    {#if cell.key === "change"}
      <DeltaIndicator value={cell.value} format="percent" threshold={0.005} size="sm" />
    {:else}
      {cell.value}
    {/if}
  </svelte:fragment>
</DataTable>

## Accessibility

The arrow is decorative and the visible number is hidden from assistive technology. A sentence is announced in their place: "Increased by 12.3%", "Decreased by 64", or "No change". Set `description` to override it, for example to localize it.

<DeltaIndicator value={0.123} format="percent" description="Hausse de 12,3 %" />
